{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And what great nation is there that has statutes, etc.</b> The reason you will be accounted wise in the eyes of the nations when you keep the statutes of Elohim and His teachings, is that there is no nation in existence of such a kind — one that has statutes indicating the existence of El and His ways, and righteous judgments in which there is nothing for the benefit of the judge or for the salary of their guardians and scribes, but whose entire concern is judgment and justice. As our Sages of blessed memory said (Sanhedrin 6b): מִשְׁפָּט לָזֶה וּצְדָקָה לָזֶה — judgment for this one and righteousness for that one: judgment for this one, that he restored to him what was his; and righteousness for that one, that he removed stolen property from his hand."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:23.417552363Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}